  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "src/ui/calculation-words.ts",
      "content": "Passing `undefined` always compares the expiration year with UTC, rather than the Workspace year used by `tradeSummary`. For example, at 2027-01-01T01:00Z in America/New_York, a 2027 contract omits its year here but includes `2027` in the Trade Summary because the Workspace is still in 2026. Thread the Workspace time zone through contract-label rendering and add a New Year boundary test so both names follow the same current-year rule.",
      "existing_code": "    ? `${instrument.symbol} ${summaryExpiration(instrument.expiration, undefined)} ${summaryStrike(instrument.strike)} ${instrument.right}`",
      "start_line": 18,
      "end_line": 18,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/calculation-words.ts",
      "content": "`summaryStrike` formats through `money`, which rounds to two decimal places, but valid option strikes support three fractional digits (`validateOptionContract` and OCC parsing). Consequently, distinct strikes such as `52.501` and `52.504` now both appear as `$52.50` in contract names, whereas the previous label preserved their identity. Preserve all significant strike digits (while padding one-decimal strikes to cents) and add coverage for a three-decimal strike.",
      "existing_code": "    ? `${instrument.symbol} ${summaryExpiration(instrument.expiration, undefined)} ${summaryStrike(instrument.strike)} ${instrument.right}`",
      "start_line": 18,
      "end_line": 18,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    }
  ],
